#import "../template.typ": somatic_page

// PAGE 6: THE GARDEN OF THE SOUL - Prompt Introduction
// Deep theoretical foundation using Shadow Work Philosopher framework
// Mirroring + Botanical metaphor

#somatic_page(
  title: "The Garden of the Soul",
  body_text: [
    Perhaps there's a heaviness in your chest right now, or a subtle resistance as you turn these pages. That is not weakness—that is *discernment*. Your nervous system is scanning: *Is it safe to look?*
    
    #v(1cm)
    
    #rect(fill: rgb("#F5F5F0"), stroke: 0.5pt + gray, inset: 15pt, radius: 2pt)[
      Carl Jung spoke of the psyche as a *garden*, not a battlefield. The shadow is not an enemy to be conquered but soil to be tended. Within it grow both poison and medicine—nightshade and iris, thorn and bloom. To integrate the shadow is not to "fix" yourself. It is to become a gardener of your own depths.
      
      The alchemists understood this. They knew that *calcination*—the burning away of impurities—must precede *conjunction*, the sacred marriage of opposites. You cannot skip the fire. You cannot shortcut to gold. The shadow demands that you feel what you have spent a lifetime avoiding, and only then does transformation become possible.
      
      This journal uses *botanical metaphors* as a somatic language. When we ask, "Where does shame live in your body?" we are not speaking poetically. We are asking you to locate the *sensation*—the tightness, the heat, the numbness—and then to name it with an image your nervous system can process. A strangler vine. A wilted lily. A birdcage of living roots.
      
      This is how the unconscious speaks. Not in concepts, but in *symbols*. Not in thoughts, but in *sensations*.
    ]
    
    #v(1cm)
    
    #align(center)[
      ◈ · ✦ · ◈
    ]
    
    #v(1cm)
    
    The pages ahead will guide you through nine phases of integration. Each phase follows a rhythm:
    
    1. *Intro*: The psychological theory and somatic science.
    2. *Prompts*: Structured, fill-in-the-blank exercises that lower resistance.
    3. *Somatic Map*: A body silhouette where you mark sensations with botanical symbols.
    4. *Ritual*: An embodied practice to release or integrate what you've uncovered.
    
    This is not linear. You may need to return to Phase 2 while working on Phase 7. That is not regression—that is *spiraling deeper*.
  ],
  image_path: none,
  layout_style: "bottom"
)
